    "narrative": "For the May 21st slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 85.94 efficiency score, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA) and a prime spot in the two-hole. **Carroll** remains our primary engine for stolen bases, and given the team's emphasis on speed, his top-tier projection makes him a lock for the OF1 slot. **James Wood** (62.77) also grades out strongly as a leadoff hitter; despite facing a lefty in David Peterson, **Wood**\u2019s underlying xwOBA of 0.381 indicates he is undervalued by the base projection, making him a high-floor start today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved choosing between the marginal outputs of **Tyler Soderstrom** (56.73) and **Austin Riley** (55.56). While **Riley**\u2019s score is weighed down by a poor 34 PA BvP history against Domingo Alcantara, his pedigree keeps him in the lineup over bench options like **Seiya Suzuki** or **Giancarlo Stanton**, who are inactive today. We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Mickey Moniak** closely; both are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and should their projected spots in the order shift downward, their efficiency scores will drop below the startable threshold, forcing us to pivot to the depth provided by **Dalton Rushing** or **Carson Williams**.\n\nRisks remain on the periphery, particularly regarding our UTIL slot, where **Kyle Karros** (55.22) is riding a slim margin to remain active. We are keeping **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, and **Zach McKinstry** on high alert should weather or late lineup scratches materialize. With **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story** still on the IL and **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang** without a scheduled game, our roster flexibility is limited. We need **Travis Bazzana** (49.78) to capitalize on his +7% platoon advantage today to keep the momentum going for the squad, as we remain committed to maximizing our stolen base potential in every slot where **Alex 